The constellation we were looking for is Cygnus also known as the Swan
It's brightest star is Deneb which is actually one of the brightest stars in the night sky
Cygnus flies along the Milky Way
Cygnus is also known as Leda's Swan; this swan is a transformed Zeus who fathered both Pollux, Clytemnestra, and Helen with Leda
As you can see, Zeus' presence or influence was seen through most of the constellation stories
A lot of information is shared and overlapping
The ancient world was messy
